[0.000, "o", "[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(git config user.name)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 4 files \u001b[37m(README.md, README.md, README.md, +1)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 6s, 305 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  To define the hardware contract for the custom board configuration, how is the breadboard wired to the Seeed Studio\r\n  XIAO RP2350? Specifically:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. Which analog pin (D0/A0 \u001b[94mGPIO26\u001b[m, D1/A1 \u001b[94mGPIO27\u001b[m, or D2/A2 \u001b[94mGPIO28\u001b[m) is connected to the potentiometer wiper, and what\r\n  reference voltage range is it sweeping?\u001b[K\r\n  2. Which 6 pins are connected to the discrete LEDs (ordered from the lowest bar segment to the highest), and are\u001b[K\r\n  the LEDs wired active-high (sourcing current from GPIO to GND) or active-low (sinking current from 3V3 into GPIO)?\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> Please layout the connections "]
