[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\n\n\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[35A\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 1m 7s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial investigation requires understanding the current workspace and configuration. Examinin...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(git config user.name)\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[26D\u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 4 files \u001b[37m(README.md, README.md, README.md, +1)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 6s, 305 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  To define the hardware contract for the custom board configuration, how is the breadboard wired to the Seeed Studio\r\n  XIAO RP2350? Specifically:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. Which analog pin (D0/A0 \u001b[94mGPIO26\u001b[m, D1/A1 \u001b[94mGPIO27\u001b[m, or D2/A2 \u001b[94mGPIO28\u001b[m) is connected to the potentiometer wiper, and what\r\n  reference voltage range is it sweeping?\u001b[K\r\n  2. Which 6 pins are connected to the discrete LEDs (ordered from the lowest bar segment to the highest), and are\r\n  the LEDs wired active-high (sourcing current from GPIO to GND) or active-low (sinking current from 3V3 into GPIO)?\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m─────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "───────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> Please layout the connections as you see fit. I'll ask you to design the breadboard layout as part of this exercise.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 4.5s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Examining the board definition files to understand pin assignments, specifically avoiding confl...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 3 files \u001b[37m(README.md, board.h, rp23xx_pico.h)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 11s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  For the breadboard layout, we can place the potentiometer wiper on \u001b[94mD0/A0\u001b[m (\u001b[94mGPIO26\u001b[m, \u001b[94mADC0\u001b[m sweeping \u001b[94m0V\u001b[m to \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m) at the\r\n  top-left pin, and wire the 6 LEDs active-high (with series resistors to \u001b[94mGND\u001b[m) along the remaining pins on the left\u001b[K\r\n  header (\u001b[94mD1\u001b[m–\u001b[94mD6\u001b[m: \u001b[94mGPIO27\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO28\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO5\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO6\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO7\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO0\u001b[m) since the console runs over USB-C rather than h"]
