[0.468, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[33A\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 4.5s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Examining the board definition files to understand pin assignments, specifically avoiding confl...)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[1;33mExplored\u001b[m 3 files \u001b[37m(\u001b[m\u001b[37mREADME.md, board.h, rp23xx_pico.h\u001b[m\u001b[37m)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 11s, 907 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\n  For the breadboard layout, we can place the potentiometer wiper on \u001b[94mD0/A0\u001b[m (\u001b[94mGPIO26\u001b[m, \u001b[94mADC0\u001b[m sweeping \u001b[94m0V\u001b[m to \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m) at the\r\n  top-left pin, and wire the 6 LEDs active-high (with series resistors to \u001b[94mGND\u001b[m) along the remaining pins on the left\r\n  header (\u001b[94mD1\u001b[m–\u001b[94mD6\u001b[m: \u001b[94mGPIO27\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO28\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO5\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO6\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO7\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO0\u001b[m) since the console runs over USB-C rather than hardware\r\n  UART0.\r\n\n  Next concern — \u001b[1mautomatic startup vs. interactive USB-C NSH console coexistence\u001b[m:\r\n\n  If the bar graph loop runs in the foreground at boot, it will block the NSH prompt on the USB-C console"]
[0.000, "o", ";\r\n  conversely, on a USB CDC/ACM console (\u001b[94musbnsh\u001b[m), NSH normally waits for a USB host connection before executing\r\n  \u001b[94m/etc/init.d/rcS\u001b[m, which would delay the LED bar graph from working when powered from a standalone USB power supply\r\n  without a host PC terminal open.\r\n\n  Should the bar graph run immediately at power-on even before a USB-C serial terminal is attached (for example,\r\n  spawned in the background during board/app initialization or without waiting for USB console connection), while\r\n  still leaving the NSH prompt interactive when a USB-C terminal connects?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> Spawn in the background, leaving NSH available for USB-C\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 7s, 414 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\n  Next concern — \u001b[1mbar graph mapping and visual behavior\u001b[m:\r\n\n  How should the potentiometer sweep (\u001b[94m0\u001b[m–\u001b[94m4095\u001b[m a"]
[0.000, "o", "cross \u001b[94m12\u001b[m bits) translate to the 6 LEDs? For example, should it use 7\r\n  discrete digital steps (\u001b[94m0\u001b[m through \u001b[94m6\u001b[m LEDs lit) with hysteresis/filtering to prevent threshold flicker, or should it\r\n  use PWM brightness modulation on the active segment?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> PWM brighness on active segment\u001b[m\r\n⣟  \u001b[94mLoadi\u001b[90mng...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[77X\u001b[77C\u001b[33mauto\u001b[39;2m · Gemini 4 Argon · medium\u001b[m\r\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
