[0.032, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[33A\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 7s, 414 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  Next concern — \u001b[1mbar graph mapping and visual behavior\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[K\n  How should the potentiometer sweep (\u001b[94m0\u001b[m–\u001b[94m4095\u001b[m across \u001b[94m12\u001b[m bits) translate to the 6 LEDs? For example, should it use 7\r\n  discrete digital steps (\u001b[94m0\u001b[m through \u001b[94m6\u001b[m LEDs lit) with hysteresis/filtering to prevent threshold flicker, or should it\r\n  use PWM brightness modulation on the active segment?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> PWM brighness on active segment\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 37.2s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial hypothesis: a file is automatically sourced under specific configuration conditions. C...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 12 files \u001b[37m(README.md, README.md, README.md, +9)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 9s, 750 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  E"]
[0.000, "o", "ach of the 6 pins on the left header (\u001b[94mD1\u001b[m–\u001b[94mD6\u001b[m: \u001b[94mGPIO27\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO28\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO5\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO6\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO7\u001b[m, \u001b[94mGPIO0\u001b[m) maps to a distinct RP2350\r\n  hardware PWM slice/channel comparator (\u001b[94mPWM5B\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPWM6A\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPWM2B\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPWM3A\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPWM3B\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPWM0A\u001b[m), so all 6 LEDs can be driven by\u001b[K\n\u001b[99D(100% duty for lower segments, proportional PWM duty on the active segment, and 0% duty for upper\u001b[K\r\n  segments).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Next concern — \u001b[1minteractive NSH command interface\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[K\n  When a user connects to the USB-C NSH console while the bar graph daemon is already running in the background, what\r\n  commands or diagnostics should they be able to run from the NSH prompt (for example, \u001b[94mbargraph status\u001b[m to inspect\u001b[K\r\n  current ADC/PWM readings, \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m/\u001b[94mstart\u001b[m, or live stream/test modes), or does the app only need to run as a\r\n  background daemon without interactive subcommands?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m─────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "───────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> bargraph start, stop, and status all sound like good commands to have. Any other options?\u001b[m\r\n⣯  \u001b[90mInitial suspicion wa\u001b[94ms a c\u001b[90mache miss, but traces show database latency is the actual bottleneck. Investigating if op...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /diff to view uncommitted changes in your workspace.\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[61D\u001b[?2026l"]
