[0.033, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[33ANext concern — \u001b[1minteractive NSH command interface\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[K\n  When a user connects to the USB-C NSH console while the bar graph daemon is already running in the background, what\r\n  commands or diagnostics should they be able to run from the NSH prompt (for example, \u001b[94mbargraph status\u001b[m to inspect\u001b[K\r\n  current ADC/PWM readings, \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m/\u001b[94mstart\u001b[m, or live stream/test modes), or does the app only need to run as a\r\n  background daemon without interactive subcommands?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> bargraph start, stop, and status all sound like good commands to have. Any other options?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 6s, 146 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  Beyond \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m, two subcommands have practical value during breadboard bring-up, while others add\r\n  complexity without clear "]
[0.000, "o", "payoff:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph test\u001b[39;1m (Hardware self-test sweep)\u001b[m: Sweeps the bar graph smoothly from 0% to 100% and back once\r\n  (temporarily pausing ADC polling if the daemon is running). This isolates LED wiring and PWM slice/channel\r\n  configuration from ADC/potentiometer wiring bugs during initial breadboard bring-up.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph set <0..100>\u001b[39;1m (Manual override)\u001b[m: Pauses ADC polling and locks the bar graph to a fixed percentage so you\r\n  can verify a specific segment's PWM brightness or measure current draw with a multimeter.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  By contrast, subcommands like runtime pin remapping, live continuous terminal plotting (\u001b[94mmonitor\u001b[m), or runtime filter\r\n  tuning add state synchronization overhead and terminal spam without solving a real problem for a 6-LED breadboard\u001b[K\r\n  target.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Would you like to include \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m and/or \u001b[94mset\u001b[m alongside \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m, or keep the CLI strictly to \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m,\r\n  \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and "]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> add test and set. Is there a path out of setting the bargraph back to sensing the pot's value?\u001b[m\r\n⢿  \u001b[90mInvestigating the build system: the configuration maintains an out-of-tree directory `xiao-rp2350-b\u001b[94margra\u001b[90mph/` along...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: When rejecting an edit, press tab to amend with feedback explaining why.\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[77D\u001b[?2026l"]
