[0.066, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[33Acan verify a specific segment's PWM brightness or measure current draw with a multimeter.\r\n\u001b[K\n  By contrast, subcommands like runtime pin remapping, live continuous terminal plotting (\u001b[94mmonitor\u001b[m), or runtime filter\r\n  tuning add state synchronization overhead and terminal spam without solving a real problem for a 6-LED breadboard\r\n  target.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Would you like to include \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m and/or \u001b[94mset\u001b[m alongside \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m, or keep the CLI strictly to \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m,\r\n  \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m?\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> add test and set. Is there a path out of setting the bargraph back to sensing the pot's value?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 9s, 724 tokens\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n  Yes — if the background daemon owns the PWM devices and operates as a state machine (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m, \u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[94mMANUAL\u001b[m, \u001b[94mTEST\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSTOPPED\u001b[m):\r\n\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph set <0..100>\u001b[m switches the daemon into \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode (pausing ADC polling and holding the requested bar\u001b[K\r\n  level, or spawning the daemon in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode if it was stopped).\n\u001b[52D\u001b[94mtart\u001b[m switches the daemon back into \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode (resuming continuous potentiometer ADC polling) if it is\r\n  currently in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode, or spawns it in \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode if stopped.\u001b[K\n\u001b[52D\u001b[94mtest\u001b[m runs one 0%→100%→0% sweep and then automatically returns the daemon to whichever mode (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m or\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m) was active before \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m was invoked.\u001b[K\n\u001b[32D\u001b[94mstop\u001b[m sets all 6 PWM outputs to 0% duty, closes the devices, and terminates the background daemon.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Would you prefer \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m to double as the command that returns from \u001b[94mset\u001b[m back to potentiometer sensing, or\r\n  would you rather have an explicit \u001b[94mbargraph auto\u001b[m (or \u001b[94mresume\u001b[m) subcommand?\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m───"]
[0.000, "o", "─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> both start resuming and an explicit bargraph resume command. User friendlyness for the win.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExploring\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(CMakeLists.txt)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[3Z\u001b[90m a\u001b[94mll bu\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[37D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[33A  configuration from ADC/potentiometer wiring bugs during initial breadboard bring-up.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph set <0..100>\u001b[m\u001b[1m (Manual override)\u001b[m: Pauses ADC polling and locks the bar graph to a fixed percentage so you\u001b[K\r\n  can verify a specific segment's PWM brightness or measure current draw with a multimeter.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\n  By contrast, subcommands like runtime pin remapping, live continuous terminal plotting (\u001b[94mmonitor\u001b[m), or runtime filter\r\n  tuning add state synchronization overhead and terminal spam without solving a real problem for a 6-LED breadboard\r\n  target.\r\n\n  Would you like to include \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m and/or \u001b[94mset\u001b[m alongside \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m, or keep the CLI strictly to \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m,\r\n  \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> add test and set. Is"]
[0.000, "o", " there a path out of setting the bargraph back to sensing the pot's value?\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 9s, 724 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\n  Yes — if the background daemon owns the PWM devices and operates as a state machine (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m, \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m, \u001b[94mTEST\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSTOPPED\u001b[m):\r\n\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph set <0..100>\u001b[m switches the daemon into \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode (pausing ADC polling and holding the requested bar\r\n  level, or spawning the daemon in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode if it was stopped).\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m switches the daemon back into \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode (resuming continuous potentiometer ADC polling) if it is\r\n  currently in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode, or spawns it in \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode if stopped.\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph test\u001b[m runs one 0%→100%→0% sweep and then automatically returns the daemon to whichever mode (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m or\r\n  \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m) was active before \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m was invoked.\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m sets all 6 PWM outputs to 0% duty, closes the devices, and terminates the background daemon.\r\n\n "]
