[0.000, "o", ">\u001b[m switches the daemon into \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode (pausing ADC polling and holding the requested bar\r\n  level, or spawning the daemon in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode if it was stopped).\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m switches the daemon back into \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode (resuming continuous potentiometer ADC polling) if it is\r\n  currently in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode, or spawns it in \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode if stopped.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph test\u001b[m runs one 0%→100%→0% sweep and then automatically returns the daemon to whichever mode (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m or\r\n  \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m) was active before \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m was invoked.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m sets all 6 PWM outputs to 0% duty, closes the devices, and terminates the background daemon.\r\n\u001b[K\n  Would you prefer \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m to double as the command that returns from \u001b[94mset\u001b[m back to potentiometer sensing, or\r\n  would you rather have an explicit \u001b[94mbargraph auto\u001b[m (or \u001b[94mresume\u001b[m) subcommand?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m───────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "─────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> both start resuming and an explicit bargraph resume command. User friendlyness for the win.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 35.8s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(NuttX supports out-of-tree builds. It's important to clarify if the approach maintains a clear...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 2 files \u001b[37m(CMakeLists.txt, Make.defs)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n⣯  \u001b[90mReading file\u001b[94m...\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────"]
