[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[31A  tuning add state synchronization overhead and terminal spam without solving a real problem for a 6-LED breadboard\u001b[K\r\n  target.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  Would you like to include \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m and/or \u001b[94mset\u001b[m alongside \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m, or keep the CLI strictly to \u001b[94mstart\u001b[m,\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mstop\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mstatus\u001b[m?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> add test and set. Is there a path out of setting the bargraph back to sensing the pot's value?\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 9s, 724 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\n  Yes — if the background daemon owns the PWM devices and operates as a state machine (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m, \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m, \u001b[94mTEST\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSTOPPED\u001b[m):\r\n\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph set <0..100>\u001b[m switches the daemon into \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode (pausing ADC polling and holding the requested bar\r\n  level, or spawning the daemon"]
[0.000, "o", " in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode if it was stopped).\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m switches the daemon back into \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode (resuming continuous potentiometer ADC polling) if it is\r\n  currently in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode, or spawns it in \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode if stopped.\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph test\u001b[m runs one 0%→100%→0% sweep and then automatically returns the daemon to whichever mode (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m or\r\n  \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m) was active before \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m was invoked.\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m sets all 6 PWM outputs to 0% duty, closes the devices, and terminates the background daemon.\r\n\n  Would you prefer \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m to double as the command that returns from \u001b[94mset\u001b[m back to potentiometer sensing, or\r\n  would you rather have an explicit \u001b[94mbargraph auto\u001b[m (or \u001b[94mresume\u001b[m) subcommand?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> both start resum"]
[0.000, "o", "ing and an explicit bargraph resume command. User friendlyness for the win.\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 1m 3s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(The `.gitignore` file contains an interesting exclusion rule referencing an environment variab...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 22 files \u001b[37m(CMakeLists.txt, Make.defs, Make.defs, +19)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[33m○\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mAskQuestion\u001b[37;22m(Anchored feature hypothesis: Build an out-of-tree custom board and user-space application in xiao-rp2350-\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37mbargraph/ (leaving nuttx/ and apps/ unmodified) for a breadboarded Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 with a potentiometer on\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37mD0/A0 (GPIO26, ADC0) and 6 active-high LEDs on D1-D6 (GPIO27, GPIO28, GPIO5, GPIO6, GPIO7, GPIO0) driven via hardware\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37mPWM slices (PWM5B, PWM6A, PWM2B, PWM3A, PWM3B, PWM0A) with proportional PWM brightness on the active bar segment. The\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37mbar graph daemon spawns automatically in the background at power-on without waiting for a USB host connection, while\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37mexposing an inte"]
[0.000, "o", "ractive USB-C CDC/ACM NSH console supporting bargraph start, stop, status, test, set <0..100>, and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37mresume. How would you like to proceed?)\u001b[m\r\n⣷  \u001b[90mAnalyzing the require\u001b[94mments\u001b[90m, the goal is to implement a bar graph visualization using PWM on an embedded system, co...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "──────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[77X\u001b[77C\u001b[33mauto\u001b[39;2m · Gemini 4 Argon · medium\r\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
