[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[33A  • \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m sets all 6 PWM outputs to 0% duty, closes the devices, and terminates the background daemon.\r\n\u001b[K\n  Would you prefer \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m to double as the command that returns from \u001b[94mset\u001b[m back to potentiometer sensing, or\r\n  would you rather have an explicit \u001b[94mbargraph auto\u001b[m (or \u001b[94mresume\u001b[m) subcommand?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> both start resuming and an explicit bargraph resume command. User friendlyness for the win.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 1m 19s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(The configuration indicates a custom board directory. Examining the relevant `Config.mk` line...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 22 files \u001b[37m(CMakeLists.txt, Make.defs, Make.defs, +19)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33;1m?\u001b[m Anchored feature hypothesis: Build an out-of-tree custom boar"]
[0.000, "o", "d and user-space application in xiao-rp2350-bargraph/\r\n(leaving nuttx/ and apps/ unmodified) for a breadboarded Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 with a potentiometer on D0/A0\r\n(GPIO26, ADC0) and 6 active-high LEDs on D1-D6 (GPIO27, GPIO28, GPIO5, GPIO6, GPIO7, GPIO0) driven via hardware PWM\r\nslices (PWM5B, PWM6A, PWM2B, PWM3A, PWM3B, PWM0A) with proportional PWM brightness on the active bar segment. The bar\r\ngraph daemon spawns automatically in the background at power-on without waiting for a USB host connection, while\u001b[K\r\nexposing an interactive USB-C CDC/ACM NSH console supporting bargraph start, stop, status, test, set <0..100>, and\r\nresume. How would you like to proceed?\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33;1mQuestion\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "───────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[1mQuestion 1/1: Anchored feature hypothesis: Build an out-of-tree custom board and user-space application in xiao-rp2350-\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mbargraph/ (leaving nuttx/ and apps/ unmodified) for a breadboarded Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 with a potentiometer on\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mD0/A0 (GPIO26, ADC0) and 6 active-high LEDs on D1-D6 (GPIO27, GPIO28, GPIO5, GPIO6, GPIO7, GPIO0) driven via hardware\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mPWM slices (PWM5B, PWM6A, PWM2B, PWM3A, PWM3B, PWM0A) with proportional PWM brightness on the active bar segment. The\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mbar graph daemon spawns automatically in the background at power-on without waiting for a USB host connection, while\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mexposing an interactive USB-C CDC/ACM NSH console supporting bargraph start, stop, status, test, set <0..100>, and\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mresume. How would you like to proceed?\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[94m> 1. Review with Goldfishes\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. Clarify additional constraints or assumptions in chat\r\n  3. Write-in...\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;"]
[0.000, "o", "22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1menter\u001b[90;22m Select · \u001b[94;1mesc\u001b[90;22m Skip\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
