[0.019, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[30A\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[0 q\u001b[J\u001b[34;1m> add test and set. Is there a path out of setting the bargraph back to sensing the pot's value?\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 9s, 724 tokens\u001b[m\r\n\n  Yes — if the background daemon owns the PWM devices and operates as a state machine (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m, \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m, \u001b[94mTEST\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSTOPPED\u001b[m):\r\n\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph set <0..100>\u001b[m switches the daemon into \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode (pausing ADC polling and holding the requested bar\r\n  level, or spawning the daemon in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode if it was stopped).\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m switches the daemon back into \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode (resuming continuous potentiometer ADC polling) if it is\r\n  currently in \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m mode, or spawns it in \u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m mode if stopped.\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph test\u001b[m runs one 0%→100%→0% sweep and then automat"]
[0.000, "o", "ically returns the daemon to whichever mode (\u001b[94mAUTO\u001b[m or\r\n  \u001b[94mMANUAL\u001b[m) was active before \u001b[94mtest\u001b[m was invoked.\r\n  • \u001b[94mbargraph stop\u001b[m sets all 6 PWM outputs to 0% duty, closes the devices, and terminates the background daemon.\r\n\n  Would you prefer \u001b[94mbargraph start\u001b[m to double as the command that returns from \u001b[94mset\u001b[m back to potentiometer sensing, or\r\n  would you rather have an explicit \u001b[94mbargraph auto\u001b[m (or \u001b[94mresume\u001b[m) subcommand?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> both start resuming and an explicit bargraph resume command. User friendlyness for the win.\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 1m 19s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(The configuration indicates a custom board directory. Examining the relevant `Config.mk` line...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 22 files \u001b[37m(CMakeLists.txt, Make.defs, Make.defs, +19)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to e"]
[0.000, "o", "xpand)\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[33;1m?\u001b[m Anchored feature hypothesis: Build an out-of-tree custom board and user-space application in xiao-rp2350-bargraph/\r\n(leaving nuttx/ and apps/ unmodified) for a breadboarded Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350 with a potentiometer on D0/A0\r\n(GPIO26, ADC0) and 6 active-high LEDs on D1-D6 (GPIO27, GPIO28, GPIO5, GPIO6, GPIO7, GPIO0) driven via hardware PWM\r\nslices (PWM5B, PWM6A, PWM2B, PWM3A, PWM3B, PWM0A) with proportional PWM brightness on the active bar segment. The bar\r\ngraph daemon spawns automatically in the background at power-on without waiting for a USB host connection, while\r\nexposing an interactive USB-C CDC/ACM NSH console supporting bargraph start, stop, status, test, set <0..100>, and\r\nresume. How would you like to proceed?\r\n\u001b[34;1m> Review with Goldfishes\u001b[m\r\n⣽  \u001b[90mWorking.\u001b[94m..\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
