[0.000, "o", "Risks Raised by the Goldfish Review\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mUpstream \u001b[94;22mrp23xx_pwm.c\u001b[39;1m 16-bit Duty Truncation & Shared Slice 3 (\u001b[94;22mD4\u001b[39;1m/\u001b[94;22mD5\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk48ed9ff56fc33038;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_pwm.h#L52\u0007nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_pwm.h:52\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 stores duty cycle as \u001b[94muint16_t\u001b[m rather than \u001b[94mub16_t\u001b[m (\u001b[94muint32_t\u001b[m), so\r\n\u001b[6Cpassing standard NuttX \u001b[94mb16ONE\u001b[m (\u001b[94m0x10000\u001b[m = 100%) truncates to \u001b[94m0x0000\u001b[m and turns the LED off at full scale.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C• \u001b[94mrp23xx_pwm.c\u001b[m also ignores \u001b[94mchannels[i].channel\u001b[m and hardcodes \u001b[94mchannels[0]\u001b[m to PWM channel A and \u001b[94mchannels[1]\u001b[m to\r\n\u001b[6CPWM channel B, with \u001b[94mD4\u001b[m (\u001b[94mGPIO6\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPWM3A\u001b[m) and \u001b[94mD5\u001b[m (\u001b[94mGPIO7\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPWM3B\u001b[m) sharing \u001b[94m/dev/pwm3\u001b[m.\u001b[K\n\u001b[78D• \u001b[3mProposed\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n⣯ \n\n\u001b[?2026l"]
